erns covering classes, extended classes, named groups, recursion and escapes; compiled bytecode compared byte-for-byte via `PCRE2_INFO_SIZE` + code copy | [ ] |\n\n### D. Context create / copy / free / set\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|---------------|-----|\n| 28 | `pcre2_general_context_create` + `_copy` + `_free` | default and custom malloc/free with user data | [ ] |\n| 29 | `pcre2_compile_context_create` + `_copy` + `_free` | `NULL` gcontext and custom gcontext | [ ] |\n| 30 | `pcre2_match_context_create` + `_copy` + `_free` | `NULL` and custom gcontext | [ ] |\n| 31 | `pcre2_convert_context_create` + `_copy` + `_free` | `NULL` and custom gcontext | [ ] |\n| 32 | `_pcre2_default_compile_context_8` / `_default_match_context_8` / `_default_convert_context_8` | exported default context contents — field-by-field | [ ] |\n| 33 | `pcre2_set_bsr` | both valid values, observed through `PCRE2_INFO_BSR` after compile | [ ] |\n| 34 | `pcre2_set_newline` | all 6 valid values, observed through `PCRE2_INFO_NEWLINE` and matching behaviour of `.`/`$`/`\\R` | [ ] |\n| 35 | `pcre2_set_max_pattern_length` | 0, 1, exact patlen, huge | [ ] |\n| 36 | `pcre2_set_max_pattern_compiled_length` | 0, small, exact, huge | [ ] |\n| 37 | `pcre2_set_max_varlookbehind` | 0, 1, 255, default | [ ] |\n| 38 | `pcre2_set_parens_nest_limit` | 0, 1, 5, default 250 | [ ] |\n| 39 | `pcre2_set_compile_extra_options` | each of the 16 extra options individually + random combinations | [ ] |\n| 40 | `pcre2_set_optimize` | `NONE`, `FULL`, and each of 64..69, each verified via compiled-size / match behaviour | [ ] |\n| 41 | `pcre2_set_heap_limit` / `set_match_limit` / `set_depth_limit` | 0, 1, 10, default, `UINT32_MAX`, observed via `PCRE2_INFO_*LIMIT` and match rc | [ ] |\n| 42 | `pcre2_set_offset_limit` + `PCRE2_USE_OFFSET_LIMIT` | `PCRE2_UNSET`, 0, mid-subject, == length | [ ] |\n| 43 | `pcre2_set_glob_separator` | `/`, `\\`, `.` × glob conversion | [ ] |\n| 44 | `pcre2_set_glob_escape` | 0, `\\`, and each ASCII punctuation char × glob conversion | [ ] |\n| 45 | `pcre2_set_compile_recursion_guard` | guard returning 0 always, and returning nonzero at depth N | [ ] |\n| 46 | `pcre2_set_recursion_limit` / `set_recursion_memory_management` | obsolete APIs, verify rc and effect | [ ] |\n\n### E. `pcre2_compile` × option cross-product (compiled bytecode compared)\n\nCompiled output is compared via `PCRE2_INFO_SIZE`, `PCRE2_INFO_FRAMESIZE`, all\nother `PCRE2_INFO_*`, and — where reachable — the serialized byte stream from\n`pcre2_serialize_encode`, which contains the full bytecode.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|---------------|-----|\n| 47 | `pcre2_compile` | random patterns, no options, `NULL` ccontext | [ ] |\n| 48 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` vs. explicit `patlen`; embedded NUL in pattern | [ ] |\n| 49 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_CASELESS` alone; + `PCRE2_UTF`; + `PCRE2_UCP`; + `EXTRA_CASELESS_RESTRICT` | [ ] |\n| 50 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_MULTILINE` × all 6 newline conventions | [ ] |\n| 51 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_DOTALL` × `PCRE2_MULTILINE` × `DOLLAR_ENDONLY` | [ ] |\n| 52 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_EXTENDED` and `PCRE2_EXTENDED_MORE` on whitespace-laden patterns | [ ] |\n| 53 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_UNGREEDY` on quantifier-heavy patterns | [ ] |\n| 54 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_NO_AUTO_CAPTURE` on patterns with groups | [ ] |\n| 55 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_DUPNAMES` with duplicate group names | [ ] |\n| 56 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_UTF` on ASCII and multi-byte patterns | [ ] |\n| 57 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_UTF` + `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` on invalid-UTF patterns | [ ] |\n| 58 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_UCP` with `\\d \\w \\s \\b` and `\\p{...}` | [ ] |\n| 59 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_UCP` + each of `EXTRA_ASCII_BSD/BSS/BSW/POSIX/DIGIT` | [ ] |\n| 60 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` (implies UTF) | [ ] |\n| 61 | `pcre2_compile` | `PCRE2_LITERAL` alo