AX), set_offset_limit (0, mid, PCRE2_UNSET), set_recursion_memory_management, set_glob_separator (valid '/','\\\\','.' and invalid), set_glob_escape (0, every ASCII punctuation, 'a', 256, 0xFFFFFFFF). Assert the RETURN CODE matches, and where the setting is observable also assert the observable effect matches (e.g. via api.pattern_info after compiling, or via a match result).\n- `pcre2_get_error_message_8` (`api.get_error_message`) for EVERY error code 0..=225 and -1..=-80 with an ample buffer (compare rc AND the message bytes), and with buffer sizes 0,1,2,...,len+2 for several codes to cover the truncation path (ERRORS rows 253-256).\n- `pcre2_maketables_8` / `pcre2_maketables_free_8` with NULL and a custom general context (compare all TABLES_LENGTH bytes); maketables_free(NULL,NULL) must be a no-op.\n- `pcre2_match_data_create` with ovecsize 0,1,2,16,1000 and NULL/custom gcontext; `pcre2_match_data_create_from_pattern` with NULL code -> NULL; get_ovector_count / get_ovector_pointer contents / get_startchar / get_mark / get_match_data_size / get_match_data_heapframes_size before and after a match (ERRORS rows 241-252).\n- passing NULL to every *_free function (match_data_free, substring_free, substring_list_free, serialize_free, converted_pattern_free, all four *_context_free, code_free, maketables_free, jit_stack_free) must be a safe no-op in both.\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n- Use ONLY `mod common; use common::*; use common::corpus::*;` — do NOT modify common/mod.rs or corpus.rs, and do NOT modify anything in c_src/. If you need a helper, define it locally in your own file.\n- Every assertion must go through `diff(label, |api| { ... Log })` (or `diff_data`). NEVER call Rust functions directly and never compare against hardcoded expectations — always C-vs-Rust through the two .so files.\n- NEVER log raw pointer values or addresses (they differ between libraries). Log pointee bytes, lengths, null-ness, and relative offsets instead.\n- Objects allocated by one library must 