{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01HD7FG93FVmBbgQ83vctkSc","type":"tool_result","content":"2196 src/substitute.rs\n//! Translated from pcre2_substitute.c.\n#![allow(unused_imports, unused_variables, unused_mut, unused_parens, dead_code)]\n#![allow(non_snake_case, non_camel_case_types, non_upper_case_globals)]\n\nuse crate::consts::*;\nuse crate::types::*;\nuse crate::macros::*;\nuse core::ffi::{c_char, c_void};\n\nuse crate::compile::_pcre2_check_escape_8;\nuse crate::context::{default_free, default_malloc, _pcre2_default_match_context_8};\nuse crate::match_data::{\n    pcre2_get_mark_8, pcre2_get_ovector_count_8, pcre2_get_ovector_pointer_8,\n    pcre2_match_data_create_8, pcre2_match_data_create_from_pattern_8, pcre2_match_data_free_8,\n};\nuse crate::match_next::pcre2_next_match_8;\nuse crate::matcher::pcre2_match_8;\nuse crate::ord2utf::_pcre2_ord2utf_8;\nuse crate::string_utils::{_pcre2_strcmp_c8_8, _pcre2_strlen_8};\nuse crate::substring::{pcre2_substring_length_bynumber_8, pcre2_substring_nametable_scan_8};\nuse crate::valid_utf::_pcre2_valid_utf_8;\n\nconst PTR_STACK_SIZE: usize = 20;\n\nconst SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS: u32 = PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_EXTENDED\n    | PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_GLOBAL\n    | PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_LITERAL\n    | PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED\n    | PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_OVERFLOW_LENGTH\n    | PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_REPLACEMENT_ONLY\n    | PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_UNKNOWN_UNSET\n    | PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_UNSET_EMPTY;\n\n/* A local memcmp(), because the C code calls the library function. Returns 0 if\nthe two byte strings of the given length are equal. */\n\npub(crate) unsafe fn substitute_memcmp(a: *const u8, b: *const u8, n: usize) -> i32 {\n    let mut i: usize = 0;\n    while i < n {\n        let ca = *a.add(i);\n        let cb = *b.add(i);\n        if ca != cb {\n            return if (ca as i32) < (cb as i32) { -1 } else { 1 };\n        }\n        i += 1;\n    }\n    0\n}\n\n/*************************************************\n*           Find end of substitute text          *\n*************************************************/\n\n/* In extended mode, we recognize ${name:+set text:unset text} and similar\nconstructions. This requires the identification of unescaped : and }\ncharacters. This function scans for such. It must deal with nested ${\nconstructions. The pointer to the text is updated, either to the required end\ncharacter, or to where an error was detected.\n\nArguments:\n  code      points to the compiled expression (for options)\n  ptrptr    points to the pointer to the start of the text (updated)\n  ptrend    end of the whole string\n  last      TRUE if the last expected string (only } recognized)\n\nReturns:    0 on success\n            negative error code on failure\n*/\n\npub(crate) unsafe fn find_text_end(\n    code: *const pcre2_real_code,\n    ptrptr: *mut PCRE2_SPTR,\n    ptrend: PCRE2_SPTR,\n    last: BOOL,\n) -> i32 {\n    let mut rc: i32 = 0;\n    let mut nestlevel: u32 = 0;\n    let mut literal: BOOL = FALSE;\n    let mut ptr: PCRE2_SPTR = *ptrptr;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01E4ym4QF9EYejzpLckvHyKE","session_id":"afdd377b-a8e3-4242-b7f7-f8439c40180f","uuid":"53de9314-99fa-4cb8-a9c4-f1f84618ca15","timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:13:39.005Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Substitute differential tests"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dmk3hse25yfl2vfbdc7xjexsw3rbaclx3jdyzxzihk3xdz6cml7q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01ByS28QCmYZoQhAvy9JHMa1","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Substring + serialize + jit tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing TWO Rust integration test files for a C-to-Rust differential verification of PCRE2.\n\nWorking dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Y8WA7r\n- C source (READ ONLY, never modify): c_src/src/pcre2_substring.c, pcre2_serialize.c, pcre2_jit_misc_inc.h, pcre2_jit_compile.c, pcre2_match_next.c, and c_src/include/pcre2.h\n- Rust crate: translation/\n\nAn existing test harness is ALREADY in place. READ THESE FILES FIRST:\n- translation/tests/common/mod.rs  (the Api struct with raw fn pointers loaded via libloading from BOTH .so files, the `diff(label, |api| -> Log)` differential assertion, `Log`, `Rng`, all PCRE2_* / ERR_* constants, `compile_logged`, `log_all_info`, `log_match_result`, `log_serialized`, `cstr`, `apis()`)\n- translation/tests/common/corpus.rs (PATTERNS, SUBJECTS, byte_subjects(), PatternGen, gen_subject)\n- translation/tests/t02_compile.rs  (an example test file — follow its style exactly)\n\nFILE 1: `translation/tests/t06_substring.rs` — differentially test every `pcre2_substring_*` function and `pcre2_next_match_8`.\nCover (CONFIGS.md rows 135-142, 179-180):\n- substring_length_bynumber for group 0..=capturecount+2, with the ovector exact / deliberately too small, and with sizeptr NULL and non-NULL\n- substring_copy_bynumber with exact-size, oversized and undersized buffers — compare the rc, the buffer BYTES and *sizeptr\n- substring_get_bynumber — compare the returned bytes and length, then substring_free\n- substring_number_from_name for existing, non-existing and duplicate names (needs PCRE2_DUPNAMES)\n- substring_length_byname / copy_byname / get_byname for unique and duplicate names, set and unset groups\n- substring_nametable_scan with and without the `first`/`last` out params (log the ENTRIES' bytes, i.e. the name-table entries the pointers point at, and their index relative to the table start — never raw pointer values), and for names that are absent\n- substring_list_get — compare the WHOLE list (every string's bytes and every length), with and without lengthsptr; then substring_list_free\n- all of the above after a successful match, after NOMATCH, after PARTIAL (PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT/HARD), and after a DFA match via api.dfa_match\n- pcre2_next_match: after a non-empty match, after an empty match, at the end of the subject, after NOMATCH/PARTIAL — compare the return value, *pstart_offset and *poptions; plus a full global-match loop over a subject driven by next_match, in UTF and non-UTF mode and with the CRLF newline convention\nUse MANY randomized patterns/subjects (Rng with a fixed seed) drawn from corpus::PATTERNS/SUBJECTS and PatternGen, plus named-group patterns you construct.\nError rows (ERRORS.md 186-203, 257-260): PARTIAL(-2), NOSUBSTRING(-49), UNAVAILABLE(-54), UNSET(-55), INVALIDOFFSET(-67), NOMEMORY(-48), NOUNIQUESUBSTRING(-50), DFA_UFUNC(-41). Also out-of-range group numbers (u32::MAX, capturecount+1) across the FFI boundary.\n\nFILE 2: `translation/tests/t07_serialize_jit.rs` — differentially test `pcre2_serialize_encode/decode/get_number_of_codes/free` and all six public `pcre2_jit_*` functions plus `_pcre2_jit_get_size_8` / `_pcre2_jit_get_target_8`.\nCover (CONFIGS.md rows 129-134, 159-165):\n- serialize_encode of 1 code and of N codes (2,3,10) — compare the ENTIRE serialized byte stream and the size\n- codes compiled with a wide range of options (UTF, UCP, CASELESS, named groups, classes, callouts)\n- with a NULL general context and with a custom malloc/free general context\n- serialize_get_number_of_codes on the produced stream\n- serialize_decode round-trip: decode, then run api.do_match with the decoded codes and compare the match results and all pattern_info; also decode fewer codes than the stream contains\n- CROSS-COMPATIBILITY: bytes produced by the C library must decode successfully in the Rust library and vice versa, and the resulting codes must behave identically. (Do this outside `diff` with an explicit two-way check; be careful to free each stream/code with the library that created it.)\n- jit_compile with PCRE2_JIT_COMPLETE, PARTIAL_SOFT, PARTIAL_HARD, INVALID_UTF, TEST_ALLOC, combinations, 0, and undefined bits — compare rc; then PCRE2_INFO_JITSIZE\n- jit_match after a successful/failed jit_compile — compare rc\n- jit_stack_create with various (startsize,maxsize) pairs including 0, startsize>maxsize, and huge; jit_stack_assign with and without a callback; jit_stack_free; jit_free_unused_memory with NULL and a real gcontext\nError rows (ERRORS.md 204-217, 261-268): NULL(-51), BADDATA(-29), BADMAGIC(-31), BADMODE(-32), MIXEDTABLES(-30) (use pcre2_maketables + set_character_tables for one code and defaults for another), BADSERIALIZEDDATA(-62) (number_of_codes<=0 in the header, and a truncated/corrupted body), JIT_BADOPTION(-45)/JIT_UNSUPPORTED(-68). Corrupt the serialized header's magic / version / config fields individually and check each yields the same error from both. Also pass negative and huge `number_of_codes` values across the FFI boundary.\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n- Use ONLY `mod common; use common::*; use common::corpus::*;` — do NOT modify common/mod.rs or corpus.rs, and do NOT modify anything in c_src/. If you need a helper, define it locally in your own file.\n- Every assertion must go through `diff(label, |api| { ... Log })`, except the explicit cross-compatibility check in file 2. NEVER call Rust functions directly and never compare against hardcoded expectations.\n- NEVER log raw pointer values or addresses (they differ between libraries). Log pointee bytes, lengths, null-ness and relative offsets instead.\n- Objects allocated by one library must only be passed back to that SAME library (the one exception is the deliberate cross-decode test, where the stream is plain bytes — copy it into a Vec<u8> first).\n- Free everything you allocate.\n- Respect documented preconditions so you don't segfault; read the C source to confirm what is legal. If a case segfaults for BOTH libraries it is an invalid test — narrow it, don't keep it.\n- Keep total runtime of each file under ~120 seconds.\n\nBUILD/RUN (must use --offline, there is no network):\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Y8WA7r/translation\n  timeout 600 cargo test --offline -q --test t06_substring\n  timeout 600 cargo test --offline -q --test t07_serialize_jit\nThe two .so files already exist at c_src/build/libpcre2.so and translation/target/release/libpcre2.so.\n\nIf a test reveals a real divergence, the RUST side is wrong (the C is always correct) — fix translation/src/*.rs to match C behaviour exactly, rebuild with `cargo build --release --offline`, and re-run. Report any Rust source fixes you made.\n\nIterate until BOTH files pass with 0 failures. Then report: tests per file, total iterations, which ERRORS.md rows you covered, and any Rust fixes."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1234,"cache_read_input_tokens":195939,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1234,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afdd377b-a8e3-4242-b7f7-f8439c40180f","uuid":"4c92c13c-ea91-48c5-ab4a-e7cbcde91440","timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:13:39.136Z"}
