{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_v5oeo2rww4zahfzey2i3e43ajnj5cfrbba46u3kngedtaknq7tqa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both files pass with 0 failures.\n\n## What was written\n\n**`translation/tests/t06_substring.rs`** — 13 tests, ~30 350 `run_case` differential cases plus the non-`run_case` tests (error paths, single-step and global-loop `next_match`). Runtime ~2.3 s.\n\n- `substring_bynumber_matrix`, `substring_option_crossproduct` — `length/copy/get_bynumber` for groups `0..=capturecount+2` plus `0x10000`, `u32::MAX-1`, `u32::MAX`; `sizeptr` NULL and non‑NULL; buffer sizes `0,1,size,size+1,size+2,64` (buffer *bytes* + `*sizeptr` compared); ovector sizes 0/1/2/3/8; compile‑option × match‑option cross product (incl. `COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT`), interpreter and DFA.\n- `substring_byname_unique` / `substring_byname_duplicates` — `number_from_name`, `length/copy/get_byname`, unique + `PCRE2_DUPNAMES` names, set/unset groups, and dup groups deliberately outside the ovector (→ `UNAVAILABLE`).\n- `nametable_scan` probe logs entry **bytes** and indexes *relative to the table start* (never pointers), with `first`/`last`, with `firstptr==NULL` (number‑query form), and for absent names.\n- `substring_list_get` — whole list: every string's exact bytes, every length, the NUL‑terminated form, and relative offsets inside the block; with and without `lengthsptr`; then `substring_list_free`.\n- `substring_after_partial` (`PARTIAL_SOFT`/`HARD`), `substring_after_dfa_match`, `substring_after_nomatch`, and two randomized tests (1500 `PatternGen` + 2000 corpus cases, fixed seeds).\n- `next_match_single_step`, `next_match_global_loops` (non‑UTF / UTF / CRLF / ANYCRLF newline conventions, invalid‑UTF byte subjects), `next_match_after_errors`.\n\n**`translation/tests/t07_serialize_jit.rs`** — 12 tests, ~2 700 encodes / ~3 500 decodes. Runtime ~0.1 s.\n\n- `serialize_encode_single_code`, `serialize_encode_multiple_codes` (N = 2, 3, 10 plus every prefix), `serialize_corpus_patterns`, `serialize_random_patterns` (1500) — the **entire** byte stream and size compared, `get_number_of_codes`, decode round‑trip with `want` = 1, k−1, k, k+1, 1000, `i32::MAX`, then `log_all_info` + 9 subject matches on each decoded code.\n- `serialize_with_custom_gcontext` — NULL vs custom malloc/free gcontext on encode and decode, plus a failing allocator.\n- `serialize_cross_compatibility` — the only check outside `diff`: asserts C‑ and Rust‑produced streams are byte‑identical, then Rust decodes C's bytes and C decodes Rust's bytes and the resulting behaviour logs are asserted equal (also against both same‑library round trips), for single‑ and 5‑code streams. Streams copied into 8‑byte‑aligned `Vec<u64>` buffers; each stream/code freed by its creating library.\n- `jit_compile_options`, `jit_match_variants`, `jit_stack_and_misc` — all 24 option sets incl. `TEST_ALLOC`, combinations, 0 and undefined bits; `INFO_JITSIZE` after each; the `PCRE2_JIT_INVALID_UTF → PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` side effect observed via `INFO_ALLOPTIONS`; `jit_stack_create` over 14 (start,max) pairs incl. 0, start>max, `usize::MAX`; `jit_stack_assign` with/without callback and NULL mcontext; `jit_stack_free`; `jit_free_unused_memory(NULL/gcontext)`; `_pcre2_jit_get_size_8`, `_pcre2_jit_get_target_8`.\n\n## ERRORS.md rows covered (verified by instrumenting the actual return codes)\n\n- t06: **186** `-2`, **187** `-49`, **188** `-54`, **189** `-55`, **190** `-67`, **191** `-48`, **192/193**, **194** `-49`, **195** `-50`, **196** `-41`, **197–201**, **202**, **203**, **250**, **257–260**. (Also observed incidentally: `-1`, `-3…-23` UTF, `-36`, `-40`, `-42`.)\n- t07: **204** `-51`, **205** `-29`, **206** `-51`, **207** `-31`, **208** `-30`, **209** `-51`, **210** `-29`, **211** `-62`, **212** `-31`, **213** `-32`, **214** `-32`, **215** `-62` (small/zero blocksize on the 1st *and* 2nd block, zeroed body, body magic, `name_entry_size`/`name_count` out of range — plus flag/table perturbations that must still decode), **216** `-51`, **217** `-31`/`-32`, **261** `-45`, **262** `-51`, **263** `-45`, **264** `-45`, **265/266** NULL, **267** no‑op, **268** JITSIZE = 0. Header magic/version/config are each corrupted individually; negative and huge `number_of_codes` are passed to `decode`.\n\n## Iterations / findings\n\n3 build-and-fix iterations. **No Rust source changes were needed — zero divergences found**; `src/substring.rs`, `src/serialize.rs`, `src/match_next.rs` and `src/jit.rs` match the C byte-for-byte on everything probed.\n\nOne test bug had to be fixed: calling `pcre2_substring_*_byname` after an *early* `pcre2_match`/`pcre2_dfa_match` argument-validation error (e.g. `BADUTFOFFSET`) segfaults in **both** libraries, because those functions read `match_data->code`/`->matchedby` before checking `rc`, and those fields are only assigned at the engine's \"fill in fields that are always returned\" point. That case is now gated by `md_code_is_defined(rc)` (documented in the file). Two other safety measures: the ovector is pre-filled with `PCRE2_UNSET` before every match so no uninitialised slot is ever compared, and a process-wide `ALLOC_LOCK` serialises the tests that install the failing allocator (libtest runs tests in parallel).\n\nI verified the differential machinery is actually live by temporarily injecting a RUST-only log byte: 9/13 t06 tests and 7/12 t07 tests reported `DIVERGENCE`; the injection was then removed.\n\nNote: other test files in the same workspace (`t05_substitute.rs`) currently fail to compile — that is another agent's in-progress file, not touched by me. `tests/common/*` and `c_src/` were not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":278155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":335,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01ByS28QCmYZoQhAvy9JHMa1","session_id":"afdd377b-a8e3-4242-b7f7-f8439c40180f","uuid":"f3b865c7-5d9a-4f3e-81a6-7878260ece16","timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:36:24.880Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Substring + serialize + jit tests"}
