{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2vccjrr2my4mxeajswmx4el2hxom65ed4ya5iospnnxzs4yygiqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `translation/tests/t05_substitute.rs` is complete and passing.\n\n## Result\n\n`cargo test --offline -q --test t05_substitute` → **37 tests, 0 failures**, 19s wall (28s with `--test-threads=1`), well under the 120s budget.\n\n## Coverage\n\n**37 tests**, all assertions through `diff(label, |api| -> Log)`. Roughly **1.71 million randomized iterations** plus ~65,000 hand-picked deterministic grid points, driving **~2.5 million `pcre2_substitute_8` invocations per library**.\n\nRandomized generators (fixed seeds `0x5AB5_0001`..`0x5AB5_0006`):\n- `sub_random_no_options` 260k · `sub_random_everything` 260k (pattern × byte-subject × replacement × option mask × buffer size × start_offset) · `sub_random_generated_patterns` 120k (`PatternGen`) · `sub_random_replacement_bytes` 650k (random bytes as replacement — hammers the `$`/`${}`/`$<>`/`\\Q\\E`/`check_escape` error surface) · `sub_random_extended_constructs` 260k (recursively generated `${n:+…:…}` / `${n:-…}` trees, stressing `find_text_end` + `ptrstack`) · `sub_random_callout_fuzz` 160k (both callouts × 5 return policies × 5 case-callout modes × random caps).\n\nCONFIGS.md rows **143–158** all covered, plus extras: `${*MARK}` against every mark verb, `\\Q…\\E` literal mode, `EXTRA_TURKISH_CASING`/`CASELESS_RESTRICT`, custom character tables via `maketables`, `match_context_copy`, `PTR_STACK_SIZE` nesting 1..14, MAX_NAME_SIZE overflow, embedded NULs, guard bytes past `*blength` on every call.\n\nERRORS.md rows **148–175** — verified reachable (I ran a throwaway probe asserting each code is actually produced, then deleted it): 148 `-34`, 149/150/151 `-51`, 152 `-41`, 153 `-71`, 154 `-72`, 155 `-73`, 156 `-74`, 157 `-33`, 158/159/160 `-48`, 161 `-35`, 162 `-58`, 163/164 `-49`, 165 `-55`, 166 `-54`, 167 `-57`, 168 `-59`, 169 (empty-match global agreement), 170 (unreachable — the C guard is `subs == INT_MAX`; substituted a 3000-substitution agreement test), 171 `-76` (+ the `-34` guard for partial without `REPLACEMENT_ONLY`), 172 `-47`/`-53`/`-63` propagated, 173 `-69`, 174 (unreachable — needs `PCRE2_SIZE` overflow), 175 `-60`. Also out-of-range option words across FFI: all 32 single bits, `0xFFFFFFFF`, `0xFFFFFFFE`, `0x7FFFFFFF` and undefined-bit combinations.\n\n## Rust source fixes\n\n**None were needed.** `translation/src/substitute.rs` matched the C byte-for-byte on every case, including `*blength`, full output-buffer contents, guard bytes, every `SubstituteCalloutBlock` field, and every case-callout argument/return.\n\n## Two test bugs I had to fix (not library bugs)\n\n1. `-47`/`-53` were unreachable with pattern `(a+)+b`: the required-code-unit start optimization returns NOMATCH before the matcher runs. Changed to `(*NO_START_OPT)(a+)+b`.\n2. `common::log_match_result` logs the **entire** ovector, but `pcre2_match` leaves it as `pcre2_match_data_create` left it on a no-match — i.e. uninitialized heap. That made `sub_matched_existing_match` fail nondeterministically (only under parallel load, when heap history differs between the two `.so`s). I added file-local `log_md` / `log_md_shape` / `ovec_snapshot` helpers that log only API-defined state (rc pairs on success, all pairs when `rc == 0`, first pair on `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`, nothing otherwise), and verify \"external match data untouched\" via a within-library before/after snapshot equality boolean. Confirmed stable over 5 repeated runs plus a single-threaded run. `common/mod.rs` and `corpus.rs` were **not** modified.\n\nI also validated the harness genuinely catches divergence by temporarily injecting an `api.name == \"RUST\"` log difference (it failed as expected) and removing it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":750,"cache_read_input_tokens":261071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":750,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01E4ym4QF9EYejzpLckvHyKE","session_id":"afdd377b-a8e3-4242-b7f7-f8439c40180f","uuid":"734bc83f-a003-4cf3-aedf-baba57255a9b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:43:54.432Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Substitute differential tests"}
