{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cb2qyjw7vyjhh6yoeapy2yccj4edy3cspisul7en7n5rlroyo2ta","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **The Rust translation of PCRE2 10.48 (8-bit, Unicode, no JIT) matches the C byte-for-byte on everything tested — zero divergences, so no Rust source changes were needed.**\n\n## Results\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` | clean (1 pre-existing unused-macro warning) |\n| Symbol parity (`nm -D`) | **143 C exports → 143 Rust exports, diff empty both ways** |\n| Undefined non-libc symbols in Rust `.so` | **0** |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row | **180/180 pass** |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row | **278/278 pass** |\n| Feature combinations | crate declares no features; both `--no-default-features` and default verified identical |\n| Test suite | **187 tests, 0 failures**, ~44 s |\n\n## Artifacts (in `translation/`)\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — all 143 symbols, mechanically from `nm -D`\n- `ERRORS.md` — 278 rows, one per distinct C rejection; plus a census showing **97 of 121** public compile error codes reached with identical code *and* `*erroroffset`, and a source-cited justification for each unreachable one (internal `PCRE2_DEBUG_UNREACHABLE` branches, 16/32-bit-only, non-Unicode-build-only, `ERR59` unassigned in 10.48)\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 180 rows across the option/shape cross-product\n- `run_verification.sh` — builds both `.so`s, diffs symbols, loops the feature power set\n\n## Tests (`translation/tests/`, 12 files)\nAll calls go through `libloading` into **both** `.so` files; nothing calls Rust directly. Comparison is byte-for-byte over: compile error code + offset, all 27 `PCRE2_INFO_*` (incl. the 32-byte bitmap and full name table), the **entire serialized bytecode**, match rc + ovector + startchar + mark + heap-frame size, every callout-block field, substitute output + `*blength`, converted-pattern bytes in all three buffer modes, and every exported data table at its exact ELF size.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n1. **Suite sensitivity was proven, not assumed.** Four mutations injected into `translation/src/` (`ord2utf` mask, `CHAR_NEL` value, a compile error code, the caseless first-code-unit flip) each made the relevant test files fail; a semantics-preserving edit left everything green. All reverted.\n2. **Some comparisons had to be narrowed to what the C actually defines.** PCRE2 leaves the ovector, `startchar` and `mark` untouched on early-return paths (`pcre2_match.c:1045-1053, 8167`), so those slots hold uninitialised heap. Comparing them was nondeterministic even C-vs-C. `defined_ovector_entries`/`mark_is_defined` in `tests/common/mod.rs` encode exactly the C-defined ranges. Cases where the C itself reads out of bounds (`NO_UTF_CHECK` on invalid UTF-8, `offset_limit` > subject length, `*_context_copy(NULL)`) are excluded and documented in `ERRORS.md` rather than tested.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1054,"cache_read_input_tokens":429558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1054,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afdd377b-a8e3-4242-b7f7-f8439c40180f","uuid":"65ac0fbf-0a5a-4cc2-99fe-69d54b685748","timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:56:33.560Z"}
